   "verified": true,
   "role": "kol",
   "wallet_id": null,
   "text": "time is an underrated part of risk management when trading lower timeframes\n\nwhen i enter a trade expecting a sharp move, i want price to react relatively quickly\n\nif Bitcoin is sitting around my entry for too long without moving in the direction i expected, i start questioning the setup\n\nthe advantage of trading lower timeframes is that you can recognize when something isn't working much earlier\n\nsometimes i'll exit a trade simply because it's taking too long to play out, even if my stop hasn't been hit\n\nprice and time both matter when deciding whether a trade is still worth taking",
   "is_reply": false,
